&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone to join our Brand Events team, which supports over 200 events each year around the world. Primarily, you’ll:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support Hudl staff attending events&lt;/strong&gt;. From small clinics in North America to larger conferences&amp;nbsp; across the world, you’ll collaborate with team members to ensure a successful event..&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Gain experience&lt;/strong&gt;. You’ll handle real-world situations, including: troubleshooting with internal stakeholders, managing an inventory of materials, and working with outside vendors.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own our event calendar&lt;/strong&gt;. You’ll be responsible for communicating with external partners and internal Hudlies on all aspects of each event.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make an impact&lt;/strong&gt;. You’ll play an integral role in ensuring our events are effective and valuable for attendees.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Location&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re currently considering candidates who are willing to work all their hours from our headquarters in Lincoln, NE along side their teammates.&amp;nbsp; Remote work is not an option at this time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Must-Haves&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A current student. &lt;/strong&gt;You’re currently enrolled in an undergraduate program, preferably a freshman or sophomore.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accountability.&lt;/strong&gt; You’re not afraid to step up to the plate and own your work.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Detailed.&lt;/strong&gt; You can pay attention to all aspects of an event to bring every piece together.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Self-motivation. &lt;/strong&gt;You have the ability to take on a project without much direction, make it yours, and see it through to completion.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Nice-to-Haves&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Eagerness.&lt;/strong&gt; You’re excited to learn new tools and add them to your knowledge toolbox.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication. &lt;/strong&gt;You have a talent for sharing information clearly and effectively.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Confidence.&lt;/strong&gt; When it comes to decision-making, you know how and when to push back on certain details for the best possible outcome.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A passion for organization. &lt;/strong&gt;You’re able to keep track of lots of information and physical materials at once.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An interest in marketing.&lt;/strong&gt; You want to gain experience testing out marketing tactics and measuring results.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
