&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.hudl.com/jobs/hudl-applicant-and-candidate-privacy-policy&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Hudl Applicant and Candidate Privacy Policy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Hudl, we build great teams. We hire the best of the best to ensure you’re working with people you can constantly learn from. You’re trusted to get your work done your way while testing the limits of what’s possible and what’s next. We work hard to provide a culture where everyone feels supported, and our employees feel it—their votes helped us become one of the &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.hudl.com/blog/hudl-2026-top-100-inspiring-workplaces?utm_medium=internal&amp;amp;utm_source=job-ad&amp;amp;utm_campaign=26_NA_talent_job-ad&amp;amp;utm_content=1org_learn-more_blog-link_learn-more_2blog_organic_3ctw&quot;&gt;Top 100 Inspiring Workplaces&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We think of ourselves as the team behind the team, supporting the lifelong impact sports can have: the lessons in teamwork and dedication; the influence of inspiring coaches; and the opportunities to reach new heights. That’s why we help teams from all over the world see their game differently. Our products make it easier for coaches and athletes at any level to capture video, analyze data, share highlights and more.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Ready to join us?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;padding: 56.25% 0 0 0; position: relative;&quot;&gt;&lt;iframe style=&quot;position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://player.vimeo.com/video/1095624224?h=9e8cdc9dbe&amp;amp;badge=0&amp;amp;autopause=0&amp;amp;player_id=0&amp;amp;app_id=58479&quot; width=&quot;&quot; height=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Your Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re hiring a Manager, 3PL Warehouse Operations to lead our global 3PL warehousing network. You’ll own our partner relationships, keep inventory data accurate across every site and make sure the gear athletes and coaches count on gets where it needs to go. You’ll also lead a team of direct reports and help them grow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As the Manager, 3PL Warehouse Operations, you’ll:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own our 3PL partnerships.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ll be the main point of contact for our global 3PL partners. That means leading operational reviews, resolving escalations and onboarding new partners from site setup to go-live.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Keep operations running smoothly.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ll oversee receiving, storage, picking, packing, shipping and returns across all sites. You’ll also plan for peak season and validate 3PL invoices against contracted rates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hold partners accountable.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ll track SLAs and KPIs, dig into performance data to find root causes and present results to Logistics leadership. You’ll also lead quarterly business reviews with the Director of Global Logistics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Protect data accuracy.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ll own inventory accuracy through cycle counting and work with our Business Operations Process Technology team on the OMS, ERP and EDI/API connections that keep inventory visible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead and develop your team.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ll set clear goals, give regular feedback and support career growth. You’ll also partner with inventory control, demand planning, transportation, compliance and accounting to keep everyone aligned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Location&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Time spent collaborating with your teammates in-person will be an integral part of your work. This role is open to candidates based in Chicago, Ill., and requires working on-site at our Chicago 3PL warehouse at least three days per week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Must-Haves&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experienced.&lt;/strong&gt; You have a bachelor’s degree in supply chain management, logistics, business or a related field and seven or more years in warehouse operations, 3PL management or supply chain logistics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A relationship owner.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ve managed external 3PL or logistics service provider relationships at a senior level. You know how to build KPI scorecards and hold partners to their SLAs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A people leader.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ve managed and developed direct reports, and you’re good at setting goals and giving feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data-minded.&lt;/strong&gt; You’re familiar with WMS and ERP platforms and EDI/API integrations. You can turn operational data into clear improvements and explain them well&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Nice-to-Haves&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Network experience.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ve managed a multi-site or multi-region 3PL network.&lt;/li&gt;
