&lt;div style=&quot;padding: 56.25% 0 0 0; position: relative;&quot;&gt;&lt;iframe style=&quot;position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://player.vimeo.com/video/1095624224?h=9e8cdc9dbe&amp;amp;badge=0&amp;amp;autopause=0&amp;amp;player_id=0&amp;amp;app_id=58479&quot; width=&quot;&quot; height=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Your Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Quality Assurance Engineer to join our performance analysis squad, a team dedicated to building best-in-class tools that help coaches and analysts turn game video and data into winning insights. You&#39;ll help us build and scale the products that power film breakdowns, tagging, stats, and reporting, so every clip, metric, and playlist is accurate, fast, and reliable. In this role, you&#39;ll lead testing efforts within your squad, focusing on both prevention and efficiency so that coaches and analysts have a seamless experience, from game day through the film room.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a QA Engineer, you’ll:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Champion squad quality.&lt;/strong&gt; Attend and actively voice quality focus in squad sprint scrum ceremonies, understand the core problem being solved and ensure backlog defects are prioritized.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive test strategy.&lt;/strong&gt; Create test plans, implement squad quality best practices, use data to drive high-quality outcomes and ensure post-mortems or root cause analyses (RCAs) are created for all hotfixes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Test and merge.&lt;/strong&gt; Leverage multiple testing approaches—including automated, exploratory and manual testing—from start to finish, ensuring sub-defects are resolved and merge builds run cleanly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Grow professionally.&lt;/strong&gt; Dedicate time to your own professional development and skill-building.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Time spent collaborating with other Hudlies in-office will be a regular part of how you work. We’re currently prioritizing applicants within commuting distance of &lt;strong&gt;Lincoln or Omaha, Nebraska&lt;/strong&gt;. You’ll be expected to work more days in-office than remote, but will have the freedom to coordinate your specific in-office schedule with your team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must-Haves&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experienced.&lt;/strong&gt; You have 2+ years of software testing experience and have worked in fast-paced environments with changing deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical.&lt;/strong&gt; You have solid experience designing and executing tests across the stack, from front-end UI validation to in-depth API testing, including proven, hands-on experience and proficiency with key languages (e.g. Python, Typescript) and modern automation frameworks (e.g. Playwright, Selenium).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mobile testing exposure.&lt;/strong&gt; You have experience testing iOS or Android applications and an understanding of mobile-specific performance, UI nuances and automation using &lt;strong&gt;Appium, Detox,&lt;/strong&gt; and/or &lt;strong&gt;React Native&lt;/strong&gt; tooling and the associated APIs that apps rely on (protocols such as GraphQL, REST, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A team player.&lt;/strong&gt; You work effectively within a global team, leading with empathy and clear communication to help your squad achieve the best outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Problem solver.&lt;/strong&gt; You can navigate technical and team challenges during changing deadlines in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Naturally curious.&lt;/strong&gt; You think outside the box by exploring creative solutions to break software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;User-focused.&lt;/strong&gt; You think critically about the user experience and easily relate to our users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Constantly learning.&lt;/strong&gt; You are passionate about learning and open to growth areas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Nice-to-Haves&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Domain experience.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ve worked in a SaaS environment or have a background in a STEM-related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI Tool Exposure.&lt;/strong&gt; Curiosity and exposure to leveraging AI tools (such as LLMs, specialized coding assistants, or test data generators) to increase efficiency in documentation, test case creation, or initial failure diagnosis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agile fluency.&lt;/strong&gt; Experience working within a Scrum framework and participating in sprint ceremonies will help you jump right in.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Our Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Champion work-life harmony.&lt;/strong&gt; We&#39;ll give you the flexibility you need in your work life (e.g., flexible vacation time, company-wide holidays and more) so you can enjoy your personal life too. Plus, every five years, we give you a paid sabbatical to unplug and recharge.&lt;/li&gt;
