&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Your Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring a Sr. Accountant, Close &amp;amp; Consolidations,&amp;nbsp; to join our Finance team, focused on executing accurate and timely month-end and year-end close processes across our global organization. You&#39;ll manage multi-entity and multi-currency accounting, partner with regional controllers, and help optimize our ERP systems as we scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Accountant, you&#39;ll:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own global close and consolidations.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll execute month-end and year-end close procedures across multiple legal entities, perform consolidation entries, and handle intercompany eliminations to ensure financial reporting integrity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Navigate foreign currency and intercompany accounting.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll oversee FX revaluations, intercompany loan accounting, and out-of-balance resolutions, partnering with tax and legal to ensure alignment with transfer pricing policies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Maintain systems and process flow.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll own the Chart of Accounts structure, serve as a functional user for ERP close workflows, and collaborate with Finance Systems to automate manual steps and improve scalability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support compliance and audit readiness.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll maintain internal controls over financial reporting, prepare audit workpapers, and collaborate with EMEA and APAC regional controllers to keep our global close process seamless.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Time spent collaborating with other Hudlies in-office will be a regular part of how you work. We&#39;re currently prioritizing applicants within commuting distance of Lincoln. You&#39;ll be expected to work more days in-office than remote, but will have the freedom to coordinate your specific in-office schedule with your team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Must-Haves&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Educated &amp;amp; Experienced. &lt;/strong&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Accounting with 5+ years of core accounting experience, focused specifically on financial close and multi-entity, multi-currency consolidations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Mastery.&lt;/strong&gt; Strong working knowledge of ASC 830 (Foreign Currency Matters), complex intercompany accounting, and multi-entity consolidation procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A process optimizer.&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on experience with ERP systems, functional close workflows, and Chart of Accounts maintenance, always looking for ways to streamline and scale processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Detail-Oriented &amp;amp; Compliant.&lt;/strong&gt; Proven track record managing foreign currency revaluations, intercompany eliminations, and maintaining rigorous internal controls for audit readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative Communicator.&lt;/strong&gt; Skilled at partnering cross-functionally with EMEA/APAC regional controllers, tax, legal, and IT teams to resolve out-of-balance discrepancies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
