&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Your Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Senior Embedded Linux Engineer&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;to work on one of Hudl&#39;s most innovative new products: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.hudl.com/en_gb/products/focus&quot;&gt;next generation, fully-automated sports cameras&lt;/a&gt;. These autonomous cameras use edge AI to automatically track the action and upload to the cloud, giving our customers seamless access to vital, real-time video and insights.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Embedded Linux Engineer, you&#39;ll:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborate.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll work closely with Hardware, Firmware and Application Software Engineers, as well as our System Architect, to build a reliable, scalable and easily updateable firmware system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead technically.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll set an example for others in planning, designing and delivering complex projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the problem.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll work in an autonomous squad that has the freedom and expertise to deliver the best solution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Power our next generation of devices.&lt;/strong&gt; Your team is responsible for turning early prototypes into fully functioning devices, working on the low-level components powering the full stack of the device.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Time spent collaborating with your teammates in-office will be a regular part of how you work. We&#39;re currently considering applicants within commuting distance of Den Bosch. You&#39;ll be expected to work more days in-office than remote, but will have the freedom to coordinate your specific in-office schedule with your team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Must-Haves&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deep embedded Linux experience.&lt;/strong&gt; You have extensive experience in, supporting and extending board support packages for hardware powered by embedded Linux, including hands-on experience with Yocto, and you&#39;re comfortable working across the full stack from kernel to user space.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Development expertise.&lt;/strong&gt; You have a strong background in user-space and BSP-level development, integration and debugging using C/C++.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Linux Kernel knowledge.&lt;/strong&gt; You understand device-tree configuration and kernel driver development, and can patch and debug drivers in vendor-supplied kernel trees.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hardware interface knowledge.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;re familiar with serial communication protocols such as UART, I2C and SPI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice-to-Haves&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Microcontroller programming.&lt;/strong&gt; You have a background in programming microcontrollers, preferably with FreeRTOS or similar RTOS environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-assisted development&lt;/strong&gt;. You work fluently with AI coding tools and can evaluate their output critically&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rust experience.&lt;/strong&gt; Exposure to Rust is a plus since a large portion of our codebase is written in Rust and we plan to extend it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wired and wireless communication protocol knowledge.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;re familiar with areas such as PCIe, I2C, UART, MIPI, Bluetooth, Wi-Fi and 4G/5G.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Camera experience.&lt;/strong&gt; Experience with cameras gives you a head start in this role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
