&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Your Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re hiring a Senior Imaging Engineer to join our optics and imaging team. You’ll own key parts of the image quality across our multi-camera systems, ensuring our cameras automatically capture high-performance footage that powers computer vision, tracking and insights for teams around the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Imaging Engineer, you’ll:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Evaluate and improve camera systems.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ll measure, analyze and improve how optics, sensors and image signal processing (ISP) perform across our computer vision applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Test and qualify hardware.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ll evaluate lenses and camera modules against optical and environmental specifications, run qualification tests and partner closely with external suppliers on technical follow-up, and refine optical test methods for both lab environments and production lines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support ISP tuning.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ll tune exposure, white balance, tone mapping and dynamic range, while contributing to camera control and 3A algorithms to enhance downstream computer vision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborate and lead.&lt;/strong&gt; You’ll contribute to imaging requirements and trade-offs alongside product managers and our optics lead, own projects end-to-end and share knowledge to mentor fellow engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Location&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Time spent collaborating with your teammates in-office will be a regular part of how you work. We’re currently considering applicants within commuting distance of Den Bosch. You’ll be expected to work more days in-office than remote, but will have the freedom to coordinate your specific in-office schedule with your team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Must-Haves&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proven imaging experience.&lt;/strong&gt; You have deep experience in imaging, camera systems or optical engineering, ideally working on shipped hardware products, bringing a strong understanding of optics, image sensors and ISP pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-on lab expertise.&lt;/strong&gt; You bring practical experience measuring image quality - including MTF/SFR, noise, color and distortion - using lab equipment like collimators, test charts and climate chambers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proficient programmer.&lt;/strong&gt; You’re comfortable using Python for analysis and tooling, as well as C/C++ on embedded Linux.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A clear communicator.&lt;/strong&gt; You explain technical trade-offs to non-specialists with ease and make sound decisions even when working with incomplete data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice-to-Haves&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Control algorithm development.&lt;/strong&gt; Experience developing camera control algorithms such as auto exposure and auto white balance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Calibration knowledge.&lt;/strong&gt; Experience with camera calibration (intrinsics, extrinsics and distortion models) and multi-camera or stitched systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Supplier collaboration.&lt;/strong&gt; Experience partnering with suppliers and manufacturing partners on specifications, sample evaluations and issue resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Embedded platform experience.&lt;/strong&gt; Familiarity with embedded camera platforms and ISP tuning tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Our Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
