&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Sr. Marketing Manager for Basketball &amp;amp; Ice Hockey is a critical pod leader and individual contributor, responsible for the strategic development, execution, and optimization of the basketball and ice hockey marketing calendar. This role&#39;s primary focus is on the North American basketball segment, driving brand awareness, increasing demand, and positioning Hudl as the go-to sports technology provider for buyers across analytics, human performance, and player recruitment personas — with secondary ownership of the ice hockey pod and its outputs. The ideal candidate is highly strategic, execution-focused, and deeply knowledgeable about the elite basketball landscape.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As the Sr. Marketing Manager for Basketball &amp;amp; Ice Hockey, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own strategy and execution.&lt;/strong&gt; Lead the marketing strategy for North American basketball and ice hockey, creating quarterly plans with KPIs to drive brand awareness, demand generation, and customer retention through integrated, multi-channel campaigns. You&#39;ll ensure this strategy aligns with overall business goals by collaborating closely with sales and strategy teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead the pod.&lt;/strong&gt; Take ownership of the basketball and ice hockey pod&#39;s output — guiding campaign development, ensuring operational excellence, and maintaining a strong go-to-market process and cross-functional alignment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Champion a test-and-learn culture.&lt;/strong&gt; Implement a test-and-learn environment where you challenge assumptions, use data to optimize campaigns, scale what works, and continuously improve our approach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner and collaborate.&lt;/strong&gt; Work with central marketing functions (web, content, social, design) and product marketing teams to deliver cohesive, high-quality outputs for product launches and feature rollouts. Maintain strong relationships with leaders in Product Management, Customer Success, and Support to ensure business alignment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manage external partners.&lt;/strong&gt; Manage external agencies in partnership with the Paid Media Manager, ensuring alignment on strategy, market insights, and performance expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Understand the customer deeply.&lt;/strong&gt; Utilize insights from Product Management, Sales, Customer Success, Support, and Decision Science to maintain a strong understanding of the elite buyer. Dive into customer research and product engagement metrics to inform the team&#39;s efforts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analyze and report.&lt;/strong&gt; Track and report on marketing performance, providing clear insights and recommendations to stakeholders based on key metrics such as CTR, CPL, CRO, and ROAS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manage budget and resources.&lt;/strong&gt; Ensure marketing budget and resources deliver positive ROI by evaluating channel mix and progress toward key business metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Location&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Time spent collaborating with other Hudlies in-office will be a regular part of how you work. We&#39;re currently prioritizing applicants within commuting distance of Lincoln, Nebraska. You&#39;ll be expected to work more days in-office than remote, but will have the freedom to coordinate your specific in-office schedule with your team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Must-Haves&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experienced.&lt;/strong&gt; You have 5–8 years of marketing experience, an understanding of marketing strategy and go-to-market approaches, and a bachelor&#39;s degree in Business, Marketing, Communications, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Basketball domain knowledge.&lt;/strong&gt; You have strong knowledge of the elite basketball landscape and the relevant buyer personas: analytics, human performance, and player recruitment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;B2B marketing expertise.&lt;/strong&gt; You have proven experience marketing to elite sports organizations in a B2B environment, with a track record of driving demand and retention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Digital marketing expert.&lt;/strong&gt; You have deep expertise in digital marketing channels including SEO/SEM, PPC, email marketing and automation, and social media, with a proven ability to devise campaigns that engage, inform, and motivate elite buyers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data fluent.&lt;/strong&gt; You have experience with web analytics applications (such as Google Analytics), optimizing campaigns through A/B testing, and leveraging data to analyze and report on performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Autonomous and operationally strong.&lt;/strong&gt; You are self-motivated with strong leadership skills and a proven ability to manage time, prioritize across a dual-sport remit, and deliver high-quality work in a dynamic organization.&lt;/li&gt;
