&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Hudl, we build great teams. We hire the best of the best to ensure you’re working with people you can constantly learn from. You’re trusted to get your work done your way while testing the limits of what’s possible and what’s next. We work hard to provide a culture where everyone feels supported, and our employees feel it—their votes helped us become one of the &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.hudl.com/blog/hudl-2026-top-100-inspiring-workplaces?utm_medium=internal&amp;amp;utm_source=job-ad&amp;amp;utm_campaign=26_NA_talent_job-ad&amp;amp;utm_content=1org_learn-more_blog-link_learn-more_2blog_organic_3ctw&quot;&gt;Top 100 Inspiring Workplaces&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We think of ourselves as the team behind the team, supporting the lifelong impact sports can have: the lessons in teamwork and dedication; the influence of inspiring coaches; and the opportunities to reach new heights. That’s why we help teams from all over the world see their game differently. Our products make it easier for coaches and athletes at any level to capture video, analyze data, share highlights and more.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Ready to join us?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;padding: 56.25% 0 0 0; position: relative;&quot;&gt;&lt;iframe style=&quot;position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://player.vimeo.com/video/1095624224?h=9e8cdc9dbe&amp;amp;badge=0&amp;amp;autopause=0&amp;amp;player_id=0&amp;amp;app_id=58479&quot; width=&quot;&quot; height=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Your Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring a Senior MLOps Engineer for our Hardware Group to build and scale the machine learning infrastructure that powers Focus, our line of smart cameras. You&#39;ll own the edge deployment pipelines that transport neural networks from training clusters to tens of thousands of devices globally, and contribute to the platform that compiles trained models into optimised inference engines for devices like the Jetson Orin, building the &quot;nervous system&quot; for the next generation of automated sports capture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior MLOps Engineer, you&#39;ll:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build scalable Edge infrastructure.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll design, develop, and maintain the delivery systems that enable us to deploy models to fleets of devices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the model compilation platform.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll build and maintain the pipeline that takes trained models and produces optimised, hardware-specific inference engines — managing TensorRT compilation, precision trade-offs (FP16/INT8), calibration, and engine validation to ensure models run reliably and efficiently on target devices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work with cross-functional teams.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll collaborate with Data Scientists, Embedded Engineers, and Product Managers to ensure smooth integration of complex features and capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive automation and reliability.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll implement infrastructure to silently test candidate models on production devices and build telemetry pipelines to monitor drift, thermal impact, and inference latency in the wild.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Solve complex physical challenges.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll tackle the unique constraints of the edge - building resilient update mechanisms for low-bandwidth environments, optimising for limited storage, and ensuring devices recover gracefully from network failures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mentor and lead.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll share your expertise to establish best practices in Python tooling, Infrastructure-as-Code, and CI/CD, guiding the team toward a more robust, automated future.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Location&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;d like to hire someone for this role who lives near our offices in London or Barcelona, but we&#39;re also open to remote candidates in the UK and Spain.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Must-Haves&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Production MLOps expertise. &lt;/strong&gt;You&#39;ve played a key role in building and operating pipelines that deploy models to production, with deep experience in CI/CD, containerization (Docker), and Linux systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative.&lt;/strong&gt; You understand that shipping to hardware is a team sport and can communicate effectively with researchers and low-level embedded engineers to translate constraints into solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Systems thinking.&lt;/strong&gt; You can design architectures that handle failure gracefully and understand the implications of deploying to 10,000 heterogeneous devices, including how to manage risk via canary releases and safe rollbacks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bias towards action.&lt;/strong&gt; You see your role as solving problems; this means filling gaps and taking initiative as needed to help the team win together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice-to-Haves&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Edge inference &amp;amp; compilation know-how. &lt;/strong&gt;You have hands-on experience compiling and optimising models for embedded hardware - ideally with TensorRT - and understand the practical implications of precision, quantisation, and engine validation at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience with our Edge AI stack.&lt;/strong&gt; Experience with the NVIDIA edge ecosystem (Jetson Orin, DeepStream SDK, TensorRT) is a huge plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Video Technologies.&lt;/strong&gt; Familiarity with video pipelines, GStreamer, or ffmpeg.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fleet management.&lt;/strong&gt; Experience with tools like AWS IoT Greengrass, Balena, or custom OTA / fleet management solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sports Passion.&lt;/strong&gt; You have an interest in sports technology, video analytics, or performance metrics—but if not, we&#39;ll teach you the domain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Our Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Champion work-life harmony.&lt;/strong&gt; We&#39;ll give you the flexibility you need in your work life (e.g., flexible vacation time above any required statutory leave, company-wide holidays, remote work options and more) so you can enjoy your personal life too. Plus, every five years, we give you a paid sabbatical to unplug and recharge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Guarantee autonomy.&lt;/strong&gt; We have an open, honest culture and we trust our people from day one. Your team will support you, but you&#39;ll own your work and have the agency to try new ideas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Encourage career growth.&lt;/strong&gt; We&#39;re lifelong learners who encourage professional development. We&#39;ll give you tons of resources and opportunities to keep growing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Provide an environment to help you succeed.&lt;/strong&gt; We&#39;ve invested in our offices, designing incredible spaces with our employees in mind. But whether you&#39;re at the office or working remotely, we&#39;ll provide you the tech you need to do your best work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support your wellbeing.&lt;/strong&gt; Depending on location, we offer medical and retirement benefits for employees—but no matter where you&#39;re located, we have resources like our Employee Assistance Program and employee resource groups to support your mental health.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Compensation&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.hudl.com/jobs/hudl-applicant-and-candidate-privacy-policy&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Hudl Applicant and Candidate Privacy Policy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Hudl, we build great teams. We hire the best of the best to ensure you’re working with people you can constantly learn from. You’re trusted to get your work done your way while testing the limits of what’s possible and what’s next. We work hard to provide a culture where everyone feels supported, and our employees feel it—their votes helped us become one of the &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.hudl.com/blog/hudl-2026-top-100-inspiring-workplaces?utm_medium=internal&amp;amp;utm_source=job-ad&amp;amp;utm_campaign=26_NA_talent_job-ad&amp;amp;utm_content=1org_learn-more_blog-link_learn-more_2blog_organic_3ctw&quot;&gt;Top 100 Inspiring Workplaces&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We think of ourselves as the team behind the team, supporting the lifelong impact sports can have: the lessons in teamwork and dedication; the influence of inspiring coaches; and the opportunities to reach new heights. That’s why we help teams from all over the world see their game differently. Our products make it easier for coaches and athletes at any level to capture video, analyze data, share highlights and more.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Ready to join us?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style=&quot;padding: 56.25% 0 0 0; position: relative;&quot;&gt;&lt;iframe style=&quot;position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border: 0;&quot; src=&quot;https://player.vimeo.com/video/1095624224?h=9e8cdc9dbe&amp;amp;badge=0&amp;amp;autopause=0&amp;amp;player_id=0&amp;amp;app_id=58479&quot; width=&quot;&quot; height=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Your Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re seeking an experienced, automation-focused Senior Quality Assurance Engineer to join our North American Sports product team. This team develops insightful analytics and Recruit products for American Football, helping high-level coaches and analysts make faster, data-driven decisions on player performance and talent acquisition.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the testing expert within your cross-functional squad, you&#39;ll own quality end-to-end — building the strategies and automation that ensure we&#39;re shipping software our users love. You&#39;ll drive quality discussions, challenge the team to maintain high standards, and be the advocate for reliability and performance at every stage of delivery.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;As a Senior Quality Assurance Engineer, you&#39;ll:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead quality initiatives.&lt;/strong&gt; Build risk-based testing strategies tailored to your squad&#39;s architecture, drive quality discussions in scrum ceremonies, challenge defect priorities, and continuously look for ways to improve practices and keep your squad&#39;s quality processes ahead of the curve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Test across the stack.&lt;/strong&gt; Design and execute tests spanning front-end UI, APIs, backend services, and data pipelines — validating transformations, service outputs, and complex logic at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Automate with intent.&lt;/strong&gt; Make informed decisions about what, when, and how to automate. Use Playwright and scripting to build reliable, maintainable automated checks that keep pace with development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mentor and grow others.&lt;/strong&gt; Use your technical depth and quality instincts to coach teammates, raise the bar for quality standards across the team, and influence how the whole squad thinks about quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally.&lt;/strong&gt; Partner closely with Engineering, Product, and Design, contribute to hiring, and invest in your own professional development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While local candidates in Lincoln and Omaha, Nebraska are prioritized, we&#39;re open to remote applicants who reside in one of the following states: Alabama, Arizona, Florida, Georgia, Idaho, Illinois, Indiana, Iowa, Kansas, Kentucky, Louisiana, Massachusetts, Michigan, Minnesota, Missouri, Nebraska, New Hampshire, North Carolina, Nevada, Ohio, Oklahoma, Pennsylvania, South Carolina, South Dakota, Tennessee, Texas, Utah, Virginia, Wisconsin and Wyoming.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must-Haves&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quality focus.&lt;/strong&gt; You see the big picture and use it to drive improvements in both quality and velocity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical depth.&lt;/strong&gt; 4+ years of software testing experience with hands-on expertise across the full stack — API testing, backend and data-heavy systems, and front-end validation — plus proficiency in automation frameworks like Playwright and languages like Python or TypeScript.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A track record of leadership.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ve owned quality for a squad, led testing initiatives end-to-end, defined success criteria, and designed approaches that measurably reduce risk in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Investigative rigour.&lt;/strong&gt; You dig to root causes of complex problems, back your findings with data, and measure outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;User focus.&lt;/strong&gt; You think critically about the user experience and let that understanding shape your testing approach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-powered working.&lt;/strong&gt; You actively use AI tools in your day-to-day workflow — for test case creation, failure diagnosis, documentation, and beyond — and look for new ways to apply them to raise the team&#39;s efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Nice-to-Haves&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance testing exposure.&lt;/strong&gt; Familiarity with load, stress, and scalability testing concepts and tools (e.g. JMeter) for validating API and backend performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sports knowledge.&lt;/strong&gt; Passion for or experience in Basketball, American Football or Ice Hockey — whether as an athlete, coach, or fan — and an appreciation for the unique challenges of sports technology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A relevant degree or equivalent experience.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;A bachelor&#39;s degree in a related field or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Our Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Champion work-life harmony.&lt;/strong&gt; We&#39;ll give you the flexibility you need in your work life (e.g., flexible vacation time, company-wide holidays and more) so you can enjoy your personal life too. Plus, every five years, we give you a paid sabbatical to unplug and recharge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Guarantee autonomy.&lt;/strong&gt; We have an open, honest culture and we trust our people from day one. Your team will support you, but you&#39;ll own your work and have the agency to try new ideas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Encourage career growth.&lt;/strong&gt; We&#39;re lifelong learners who encourage professional development. We&#39;ll give you tons of resources and opportunities to keep growing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Provide an environment to help you succeed.&lt;/strong&gt; We&#39;re always investing in our offices, designing incredible spaces with our employees in mind. But whether you&#39;re at the office or working remotely, we&#39;ll provide you the tech stack and hardware to do your best work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Take care of your mental and physical health.&lt;/strong&gt; Medical plans tailored for you and your family—including vision, dental, and fertility benefits—and stay supported with our EAP and Employee Resource Groups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contribute to your 401(K).&lt;/strong&gt; Yep, that&#39;s free money. We&#39;ll match up to 4% of your own contribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
