&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Your Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring a Senior Systems Analyst to help us manage and scale Hudl&#39;s cloud infrastructure costs and governance practices. You&#39;ll embed within our Platform Engineering team and lead our FinOps practice, owning cost reporting, tooling, and optimization work that directly impacts how we build and run software at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Systems Analyst, you&#39;ll:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own FinOps strategy and execution.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll drive cloud cost transparency, optimization, and governance across Hudl&#39;s AWS infrastructure — from setting up tooling and reporting to building a culture of cost accountability with our engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build and maintain cost dashboards.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll design and own FinOps dashboards that surface actionable insights for engineering leadership, making it easy to understand spend trends and identify optimization opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner with engineering.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll work side-by-side with platform and application engineers to identify and implement right-sizing, reserved instance strategies, commitment-based savings plans, and architectural improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Improve our tooling ecosystem.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll evaluate and manage cloud cost tools (like CloudZero) and build internal automation to reduce waste and improve efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Location&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Time spent collaborating with other Hudlies in-office will be a regular part of how you work. We&#39;re currently prioritizing applicants within commuting distance of Lincoln. You&#39;ll be expected to work more days in-office than remote, but will have the freedom to coordinate your specific in-office schedule with your team.&lt;/p&gt;
